  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Guiding National Park protection efforts via aerial surveillance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to provide support to the Gabonese National Parks Agency (ANPN) and the Forestry Department through the provision of information on human activities gathered from aerial surveys. This will be accomplished by a set of flight plans to cover bais, savannahs, marshes, park limits, and key access routes. All flights will result in GPS and high resolution geo-referenced photographs from which an observation report will be generated the same day and provided to the relevant authority in order to improve law enforcement capacity and increase protection of Gabons National Parks. Activities include: 1) Quarterly aerial surveillance of national parks&apos; savannahs ands swamps, 2) Twice yearly aerial surveys of all known bais, 3) Annual surveillance flights of boundaries of each park, and 4) Standardized data collection methods and reporting for adaptive management.</narrative>
  </description>
